[2026-11-03 00:55:35] LLM suggestion: ## Analysis

### Pareto Front Review (both objectives measured)

Filtering to experiments with both Elastic Modulus and Pore Fraction measured:

| Condition | Modulus (bar) | Pore Fraction | Quality |
|---|---|---|---|
| 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s (run1) | 936.62 | 0.27 | minor wrinkles |
| 17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s (run1) | 860.94 | 0.28 | wrinkle |
| 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s (run2) | 675.14 | 0.30 | wrinkle+gap |
| 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s (run6) | 658.85 | 0.31 | clean ✓ |
| 17-0add-15deg-90s-N2-1800s (run2) | 640.23 | 0.29 | clean ✓ |
| 18-0add-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s (run3) | 421.45 | **0.44** | minor wrinkles |
| 18-0add-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s (run5) | 468.22 | **0.40** | wrinkles |
| 17p5-15deg-200s-NoN2-1800s | 367.39 | **0.38** | clean ✓ |
| 17p5-15deg-400s-NoN2-1800s | 400.76 | **0.40** | minor fold |

**Approximate Pareto front:**
- High modulus / lower pore fraction: ~17.5 wt%, bath 18–19°C, N2, 75–90s wait → ~660–937 bar, 0.27–0.31 PF
- High pore fraction / lower modulus: ~18 wt%, bath 15°C, no-N2, long wait → ~400–470 bar, 0.38–0.44 PF

### Key Observations

1. **run1 of 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s** shows 936 bar / 0.27 PF — the highest modulus observed, but based on a single specimen (SD=0, only 1 fit survived), with minor wrinkles. This is a single-run outlier with very high uncertainty.

2. **run6 of 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s** (658 bar / 0.31 PF, clean membrane) is the most reliable high-modulus result at bath_temp=18°C.

3. **The 18-0add-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s** series (runs 1–5) consistently shows high pore fraction (0.32–0.44) but moderate modulus (340–470 bar). Run3 is the best: 421 bar / 0.44 PF.

4. **Gap in the Pareto space**: No experiment has simultaneously achieved modulus >500 bar AND pore fraction >0.36. This is the key unexplored region.

5. **Hypothesis**: The high-pore-fraction conditions use no-N2 + long wait + bath 15°C. The high-modulus conditions use N2 + short wait + bath 18–19°C. Could an intermediate condition (moderate wait, no-N2, bath ~16–17°C, polymer ~17.5 wt%) push both objectives simultaneously?

6. **Under-sampled region**: No-N2 + bath_temp 16–17°C + moderate wait (100–200s) + polymer 17.5 wt% has not been explored. The no-N2 condition with longer evaporation time tends to increase pore fraction (skin layer effect), while bath_temp 16–17°C has shown decent modulus in the N2 series.

### Recommendation

Explore **no-N2 + bath_temp 17°C + coupon_to_bath_wait_time ~120s + polymer_wt 17.5 + mixing_temp 65°C + pullcast_speed 10**. This is a genuinely novel point:
- No-N2 with moderate wait (~120s) at bath 17°C has not been tried
- The no-N2 + moderate wait combination has shown elevated pore fraction in the 15°C series
- Bath 17°C (vs 15°C) may help maintain modulus while the no-N2 + moderate wait promotes higher pore fraction
- This sits between the two Pareto extremes and could reveal whether a balanced improvement is achievable

This is distinct from all prior experiments (closest is 17-0add-17deg-75s-N2-1800s which used N2, and 17p5-15deg-200s-NoN2-1800s which used bath 15°C).

