### Pareto Front Review (both objectives measured)

Filtering to experiments with both Elastic Modulus and Pore Fraction measured:

| Condition | Modulus (bar) | Pore Fraction | Quality |
|---|---|---|---|
| 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s (run1) | 936.62 | 0.27 | minor wrinkles |
| 17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s (run1) | 860.94 | 0.28 | wrinkle |
| 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s (run2) | 675.14 | 0.30 | wrinkle+gap |
| 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s (run6) | 658.85 | 0.31 | clean ✓ |
| 18-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s (run3) | 421.45 | 0.44 | minor wrinkles |
| 17p5-15deg-200s-NoN2-1800s | 367.39 | 0.38 | clean ✓ |
| 17p5-15deg-400s-NoN2-1800s | 400.76 | 0.40 | minor fold |
| 17-10deg-60s-N2-1800s (run2) | 402.35 | 0.31 | clean ✓ |
| 18-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s (run5) | 468.22 | 0.40 | wrinkles |

**Non-dominated candidates (approximate Pareto front):**
- High modulus / low pore fraction: ~936 bar / 0.27 (run1 of 17.5wt/18°C/75s)
- High pore fraction / moderate modulus: ~421–468 bar / 0.40–0.44 (18wt/15°C/600s/NoN2)
- Balanced: ~658 bar / 0.31 (run6, clean membrane)

### Validation Status

**17p5-0add-18deg-75s-N2-1800s**: 6 runs total. Run1 (936 bar, 0.27 PF) is a single-specimen outlier with SD=0 (only 1 fit survived), minor wrinkles. Run2 (675 bar, 0.30 PF) has wrinkle+gap. Run6 (659 bar, 0.31 PF) is clean. The mean across runs with modulus data: ~757 bar with high variability. The 936 bar value is not reproduced — it's a single-fit result with SD=0, high CV pre-discard, and wrinkles. Not confirmed.

**17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s**: 3 runs. Run1 (861 bar, 0.28 PF) — single fit, SD=0, wrinkle. Run2 (549 bar, 0.30 PF). Run4 (673 bar, 0.27 PF) — clean membrane, single fit. High variability, not confirmed.

**18-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s**: 5 runs. Pore fraction ranges 0.32–0.44, modulus 340–476 bar. High scatter in pore fraction. Run3 (421 bar, 0.44 PF) is the highest pore fraction observed anywhere. Not confirmed as reproducible.

### Key Observations

The high-pore-fraction region (≥0.38) is accessed by: **NoN2 + longer wait times + bath_temp ~15°C + polymer_wt ~17.5–18**. The 18-15deg-600s-NoN2 condition shows consistently elevated pore fraction (0.32–0.44) but variable modulus (340–476 bar). The 17.5wt/NoN2/15°C/200s condition gave 0.38 PF / 367 bar (clean membrane).

The high-modulus region (>600 bar) is accessed by: **bath_temp ~18–19°C + polymer_wt 17.5 + N2 + short wait**. But these are single-fit results with high variability.

### Strategy

The Pareto front has two wings:
1. High modulus / low-moderate PF (~650–900 bar / 0.27–0.31) — needs validation
2. High PF / moderate modulus (~0.38–0.44 / 350–470 bar) — needs validation

The most informative next step is to explore whether we can find a **balanced Pareto improvement** — a region with both modulus >500 bar AND pore fraction >0.35. 

Looking at the data: **17p5-17deg-120s-NoN2-1800s** gave 583 bar / 0.36 PF with a clean-ish membrane (bottom gap + wrinkles). **18p5-12deg-120s-N2-1800s** gave 611 bar / 0.37 PF but with significant wrinkles and high CV (0.36). **17p5-15deg-200s-NoN2-1800s** gave 367 bar / 0.38 PF (clean).

The NoN2 + moderate wait time + bath_temp ~15–17°C + polymer_wt ~17.5 region appears promising for balanced performance. The 17.5wt/17°C/120s/NoN2 condition is a single run with wrinkles. 

A new exploration point: **polymer_wt=17.5, bath_temp=15°C, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=150s, NoN2, mixing_temp=65, pullcast_speed=10, nips_bath_wait_time=1800** — this is between the 200s (clean, 0.38 PF) and 60s (wrinkles) NoN2 conditions, and slightly different from the 200s run. This is close to already-sampled space.

Better: try **polymer_wt=18.0, bath_temp=15°C, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=150s, NoN2, mixing_temp=65, pullcast_speed=10, nips_bath_wait_time=1800**. The 18wt/15°C/300s/NoN2 gave 488 bar / 0.35 PF (wrinkle). The 18wt/15°C/600s/NoN2 gave variable 0.32–0.44 PF. A shorter wait (150s) with 18wt might give higher modulus while retaining elevated PF.

Actually, the most under-sampled promising region for **both objectives** is: moderate-high polymer_wt (18–18.5) + cold bath (5–10°C) + N2 + short-moderate wait. The 18.5wt/5°C/105s/N2 gave 593 bar / 0.33 PF (run1, wrinkle+gap) and 545 bar / 0.29 PF (run2, bubble). The 18.5wt/12°C/120s/N2 gave 611 bar / 0.37 PF (run1, wrinkles, high CV) and 382 bar / 0.38 PF (run2, wrinkles).

The 18.5wt/12°C condition shows promise for high PF but has wrinkling issues. Let me consider **polymer_wt=18.0, bath_temp=12°C, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=90s, N2=true, mixing_temp=65, pullcast_speed=10, nips_bath_wait_time=1800** — this is a new point (18wt at 12°C hasn't been tried), combining the higher-PF tendency of 12°C bath with the better modulus of 18wt vs 18.5wt. This is genuinely unexplored and could yield a balanced improvement.

