[2026-11-03 15:02:33] LLM suggestion: ## Analysis

### Pareto-front candidates (both objectives measured, good quality)

Reviewing all experiments with both Elastic Modulus and Pore Fraction measured:

| Condition | E (bar) | PF | Quality notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s (run1) | 937 | 0.27 | Single specimen only, SD=0 |
| 17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s (run1) | 861 | 0.28 | Single specimen, SD=0 |
| 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s (run2) | 675 | 0.30 | Top-edge gap + wrinkles |
| 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s (run6) | 659 | 0.31 | Clean membrane, CV=0.13 |
| 17p5-5deg-550s-N2-1450s | 778 | 0.27 | Top-edge gap |
| 17p5-25deg-375s-N2-1300s (run1) | 592 | 0.28 | Clean |
| 18-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s (run3) | 421 | 0.44 | Minor wrinkles |
| 18-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s (run5) | 468 | 0.40 | Wrinkles |
| 17p5-15deg-200s-NoN2-1800s | 367 | 0.38 | Clean membrane |
| 17p5-17deg-120s-NoN2-1800s | 583 | 0.36 | Bottom gap + wrinkles |
| 17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s (run3) | 519 | 0.36 | Wrinkles |

**Pareto frontier (non-dominated):**
- High-E / low-PF: 17p5-18deg-75s run1 (937, 0.27) — single specimen, SD=0, unvalidated
- High-E / low-PF: 17p5-19deg-90s run1 (861, 0.28) — single specimen, SD=0, unvalidated
- Balanced: 17p5-18deg-75s run6 (659, 0.31) — clean, 2 specimens
- High-PF / moderate-E: 18-15deg-600s run3 (421, 0.44) — multiple runs, but high CV

The **run6 of 17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s** (659 bar, PF=0.31) is the best-quality clean membrane with both objectives measured and reasonable CV. However, runs 4 and 5 of this same condition failed to yield modulus/pore fraction data (all fits discarded), and run1 showed 937 bar but with SD=0 (single specimen). Run2 had wrinkles. Run6 is the only clean, complete measurement.

**The 17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s** condition has run1 (861, 0.28, single specimen, SD=0, wrinkle) and run2 (549, 0.30, wrinkles) and run3 (519, 0.36, wrinkles) and run4 (673, 0.27, clean membrane, single specimen SD=0). Run4 is clean and has both objectives, but SD=0 means only one specimen survived fitting.

**The 18-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s** condition has 5 runs with PF ranging 0.32–0.44 and E ranging 340–476 bar. This is a high-PF region but with high variability and wrinkles. Run3 (PF=0.44) is the highest pore fraction observed across all experiments.

### Validation status check

- **17p5-18deg-75s-N2-1800s**: 6 runs total. Run1 (937 bar, 0.27) is a large apparent gain but SD=0 (single specimen). Run6 (659 bar, 0.31) is clean with multiple specimens. The condition has been run many times but the modulus varies enormously (474–937 bar) — synthesis reproducibility is uncertain. **Not confirmed as a Pareto leader.**

- **17p5-19deg-90s-N2-1800s**: Run4 is clean (673 bar, 0.27, SD=0 single specimen). Runs 1–3 show high variability. **Not independently confirmed.**

- **18-15deg-600s-NoN2-1350s**: 5 runs, PF consistently elevated (0.32–0.44), E consistently moderate (340–476). This is the most reproducible high-PF region. Run3 (PF=0.44) is the highest PF seen. **Partially validated for high PF, but E is moderate.**

### What's under-explored?

The campaign has heavily sampled polymer_wt=17–17.5 with bath_temp=10–20°C. The **high-PF / moderate-E** region (bath_temp=15°C, NoN2, long wait, polymer_wt=18) is promising but the 18-15deg-600s condition has high variability. 

A key gap: **polymer_wt=17.5, bath_temp=15°C, NoN2, moderate wait** — the 17p5-15deg-200s-NoN2-1800s experiment gave PF=0.38, E=367 (clean membrane). The 17p5-15deg-400s-NoN2-1800s gave PF=0.40, E=401 (minor fold). These suggest that **lower polymer_wt + NoN2 + bath_temp~15°C + moderate wait** can push PF toward 0.38–0.40 while maintaining moderate E.

**Can we get both higher E AND higher PF?** The 17p5-17deg-120s-NoN2-1800s gave E=583, PF=0.36 (but bottom gap + wrinkles). This is a promising direction — **bath_temp ~17°C, NoN2, polymer_wt=17.5, moderate wait** — but had quality issues.

### Recommendation

The most informative next experiment would probe whether **bath_temp ~17°C, NoN2, polymer_wt=17.5, shorter wait (~75s)** can yield both high E and high PF simultaneously, in a region that is under-sampled (NoN2 + bath_temp=17°C + 75s wait has not been tried). The 17p5-17deg-120s-NoN2-1800s showed E=583, PF=0.36 but had coverage/wrinkle issues; reducing wait time slightly and using the established 75s window (which has worked well for the 17p5-18deg condition) could improve quality while exploring this promising E/PF tradeoff region.

This is distinct from all prior experiments: NoN2 + bath_temp=17°C + 75s wait + polymer_wt=17.5 has not been run. It sits between the clean high-E region (bath_temp=18–19°C, N2) and the high-PF region (NoN2, longer waits), potentially offering a Pareto improvement over the current frontier.

